## How to Use This Scaffold

1. Make sure Viber is up (`http://localhost:8088/health`) and you have its token, if you set one.
2. Set the token as an environment variable on this machine, once. Never paste it into chat or a committed file:

   ```powershell
   [Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable("VIBER_TOKEN", "<token>", "User")
   ```

   Restart Claude Code afterwards so it sees the variable. Skip this if Viber runs without a token.
3. Open the repository in Claude Code and paste the **"Scaffold Prompt"** section (everything below the `---` divider).
4. Answer the questions. Claude checks Viber, creates what is missing, writes the files, and reports.
5. Start a **new** Claude Code session in the repo (hooks load at session start), approve the `viber` MCP server when
   asked, and run `/status`.

